# Local Permission Profile

## Preferred Profile

- For local Cubeless Windows, Unreal, and MCP work in `UnrealMCP5_6_1`, prefer the broadest local-work Codex session profile available.
- Preferred runtime:
  - filesystem sandbox: `danger-full-access`
  - network access: enabled
  - approval policy: `never` or the closest available automatic-approval mode
- This profile should be used on every PC where the user intentionally works on `UnrealMCP5_6_1`.

## Why

- `UnrealMCP5_6_1` work is expected to stay inside this repository for routine agent, MCP, build, and verification tasks.
- Unreal Editor launch, UnrealBuildTool, MCP bridge checks, and Git sync are normal local maintenance tasks.
- Restrictive `workspace-write` sessions can block valid local writes or network operations unless the repository is added as a writable root or approvals are granted.

## If Full Access Is Not Available

- Report the active permission state before broad project/MCP work.
- If the launcher supports writable roots, include the active `UnrealMCP5_6_1` repository. Add external repositories only when the user explicitly names them.
- If approvals are required, use the tool escalation flow and explain the exact local action.
- Do not pretend this file changed runtime permissions; it only records the preferred session profile.

## Safety Boundaries

- Maximum local work permission is not permission to change everything.
- Do not alter credentials, secrets, account settings, remotes, destructive Git history, unrelated dirty work, or system security settings unless the user explicitly asks for that exact action.
- Keep Git operations separate per repository.
- Keep generated Unreal assets, package outputs, `_MCP_Temp`, `_MCP_Sample`, and unrelated user work out of commits unless explicitly requested.

## New PC Setup

- Clone `UnrealMCP5_6_1` normally; the embedded `codex/` directory travels inside the same repository.
- On Windows, run `codex/scripts/grant-local-workspace-full-control.ps1` from the repository root only when ACL repair is explicitly needed.
- The permission script resolves paths from the embedded `codex` location and must not hardcode a drive letter.
- Standard setup covers the `UnrealMCP5_6_1` repository and embedded `codex/`; pass `-AdditionalRoots` only for explicitly requested external roots.
- Use `-VerifyOnly` after setup to confirm that expected roots have explicit or inherited `FullControl`.
- Start Codex from the `UnrealMCP5_6_1` repository root for MCP work.
- Choose the broad local-work permission profile during session creation.
- If starting under a restricted profile, ensure this repository is a writable root before asking for edits.
